Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:10:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] library: a Windows path typed into the MCP command field
 saves whole (#2685)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed
- words() in the Library plugin's client.js took every backslash as an
  escape, so a command typed as an absolute Windows path — the reporter's
  C:\Users\...\npx.cmd -y chrome-devtools-mcp@latest — saved as
  C:Users...npx.cmd and the server never started. A double-quoted path
  ("C:\Program Files\...") lost its separators the same way, and a UNC
  path lost its leading \\. The line is split into argv for exec, not a
  shell's words: a backslash now takes only the next blank or quote with
  it, in and out of quotes. my\ server still means one word with a
  space, and a saved path still survives its own editor through quote().

Run
- new internal/gui/tests/library-mcp-windows-command.test.cjs (Playwright,
  real page, faked API): the reporter's line byte for byte, a saved path
  reopened and saved again, a double-quoted path with a blank, a UNC
  path, a POSIX-escaped blank. On cb05dc2d before the fix both engines
  saved C:UsersxxxAppDataRoamingfnmaliasesdefaultnpx.cmd (red, en and
  zh); after, chromium and webkit are green, as are the sibling
  library-mcp-copy-config and library-servers-bulk on both engines.
- ablation: with client.js restored to cb05dc2d and the test kept, both
  engines go red again; with the fix back, green.
- node --check client.js clean. No Go files touched.

